  data: {
    LLM: "Avoid making one 'Super Hand' and one 'Trash Hand'. A balanced partition (e.g., two Flushes) is often more reliable than a single Prial and a High-Card hand.\n\nThe 'Front' Signal: If playing in rounds, winning the first hand comparison puts immense pressure on the opponent. Invest your best cards in Hand A if you intend to bluff Hand B.\n\nRange Splitting: Evaluate the total number of trumps and high cards in the 6-card deal. If the deck is 'heavy' with Spades, splitting your Spades across two hands might be a safer defensive move than one strong Flush.",
    Player: "Avoid making one 'Super Hand' and one 'Trash Hand'. A balanced partition (e.g., two Flushes) is often more reliable than a single Prial and a High-Card hand.\n\nThe 'Front' Signal: If playing in rounds, winning the first hand comparison puts immense pressure on the opponent. Invest your best cards in Hand A if you intend to bluff Hand B.\n\nRange Splitting: Evaluate the total number of trumps and high cards in the 6-card deal. If the deck is 'heavy' with Spades, splitting your Spades across two hands might be a safer defensive move than one strong Flush.",
